  "key_findings": [
    "Biological ligand sensing ('sensed by', 'recognized by') requires forward syntax (ligand -> receptor, UPREGULATES). Standard passive reversal treats the receptor as the cause and ligand as effect, causing directional inversion false negatives.",
    "Bacterial two-component systems (TCSTS) adhere to strict directional signaling flow: Histidine Kinase Sensor -> Cognate Response Regulator. Spurious reverse regulation (RR -> SK) caused by co-occurrence in operon descriptions is eliminated by the TCSTS directional invariant.",
    "Gold annotation audit identified a discrepancy in PMC1804205, where gold specifies PmrA -> PmrD but paper text explicitly and repeatedly demonstrates that PmrD activates PmrA ('PmrD, the post-translational activator of the PmrA protein'). Both original and adjusted metrics are documented."
